{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "rates-start-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.48: `rates-start`, the Rates-scale twin of `process-crankcase-start` -- THC, CO and NOx from START EXHAUST (102, 202, 302) and CRANKCASE START EXHAUST (116, 216, 316) for the gasoline-selected passenger car in Washtenaw County, road types 1 and 4, at `<modelscale value=\"Rates\"/>`.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES. A start is not per mile, and MOVES writes it to three tables, none of which `scale-rates` touches. RatePerStart is BaseRateOutput's emissionRate -- the inventory's adjusted rate over the cohort's source-bin share, per start (`rtRate_direct`), and crankcase start chained from it (`rtRate_chained`). RatePerVehicle is MOVESOutput over the cohort's population, MOVESOutput being the inventory's own quantity at Rates scale. StartsPerVehicle is the age's starts per vehicle, the same for every fuel of a model year, with a row wherever the cohort has population -- 125 rows where RatePerStart's start block has 124, because the cohort without a start rate still has starts. Measured in pandas against `process-crankcase-start` before the port: both quotients within 1.1e-05.\n\nTHE BINDINGS. The twin's, plus `n_ratesScale` = 1. `n_outputRate` = 684 is the (pollutant-process, cohort) pairs, checked by `rateSurvivorCount`.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "rates",
      "rates-start"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-start/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecyear.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, yearID 2020. The scope comes from these tables and never from the RunSpec XML, whose @key attributes are 0-based indices into sorted ID lists (docs/mixed-onroad.md §0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
